  "_syntax": "terms: words separated by spaces form a phrase; a trailing * on a word matches any ending; an Arabic word also matches after one joined prefix (و ف ب ل ك ال and their pairs, the Egyptian verb prefixes بـ هـ and ا ي ت ن); Latin words ignore case unless the rule says case: true. pattern: a regular expression over the normalised text (no diacritics, tatweel or invisible characters such as zero-width spaces, joiners and variation selectors; one alef, ى as ي, ة as ه, Arabic-Indic and Persian digits as 0-9, ٪ as %); flags i ignores case. supporting rules are reported only on a line where a rule hit. zones count for this domain. Only a closed bracket zone (﴿﴾) hides anything (a zone may say hides: false), and only other domains' plain words: a terms rule unless it says zone_hideable: false, a pattern rule only if it says zone_hideable: true. A hit, or a zone, holding a digit, % or a currency sign is never hidden; a quotation after a citation hides nothing. Detection is a hint for the reviewer, never a filter.",
